{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/364394-hunt-idea-need-antagonist","id":364394,"title":"Hunt Idea, Need Antagonist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-09T07:58:25-08:00","id":364394,"title":"Hunt Idea, Need Antagonist","content":"This is in the werewolf thread since that's what the party will be made of (not starting until 2E comes out, just getting things ready).<br /> <br /> The adventure idea is a classic one: A writer has been producing a RPG that details a werewolf society eerily similar to the real world*, and the characters are encouraged to investigate. The secret is that the writer doesn't actually <i>know</i> anything about the Forsaken, and there's nothing supernatural at play. Except for a Spirit of Inspiration supping at the essence created while he works.<br /> <br /> However, this writer has attracted <i>other</i> attention. But from what, I'm having trouble deciding. I want to just make it a Pure pack who investigated the guy, found him to be harmless, and decided to use him as bait to lure Forsaken to the area, but that doesn't strike me as a Pure plan, you know?**<br /> <br /> Ideally the antagonist would have the following features:<br /> <br /> 1) More interested in the PCs than the writer<br /> 2) Capable of detecting the PCs when they show up and determining at the very least that they aren't human.<br /> 3) Doesn't mind staying around to watch the writer and doesn't want to harm or kill him (since they would rather use him as bait or are interested in his life for other reasons)<br /> <br /> Other spirits I figure would just try to kill the spirit of inspiration and eat its corpus, though if I made it a little stronger I guess it could be the local leader of the spirit court, and perhaps one of its underlings wants to perform a coup?<br /> <br /> Crossover is fine, though I'd prefer to avoid it. That having been said, I know that the Purified are involved with spirits, so maybe one of those is skulking around?<br /> <br /> Also acceptable, what with this &quot;meta, storytelling-related&quot; plot I guess that a True Fae or an Actor could be involved. It's one of those kind of stories that I associate with Changeling games, you know? Doing this in Werewolf without reaching out to other stuff is tricky. :/<br /> <br /> * Full details: Since the game takes place in 1995, I decided that the Old World of Darkness will be an actual in-setting element, and the writer in question is Mark Rein-Hagen. I don't plan on actually trying to portray him because I think that'd be weird. So the game in question is <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>. Different enough, but still has some qualities that the Forsaken would be iffy about.<br /> <br /> ** Please correct me if I'm wrong. I don't know as much about the Pure as I should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T08:14:34-08:00","id":364414,"title":"","content":"Things have likely changed about the Pure from first to second edition, but while using bait to lure Forsaken seems like it would be their thing, investigating a writer because he's writing about werewolves in the first place doesn't, except maybe Fire-touched, to make sure they write the truth about how the Forsaken are villains.<br /> <br /> And most spirits would likely leave the Inspiration spirit alone, unless a writer's block spirit pops up. They tend to eat their nature, so cat spirits will eat mouse spirits.<br /> <br /> Anyways, this sounds like it could be azlu. They are one of the shartha, specifically the spider hosts. They weave a sort of web that thickens the gauntlet, but they also are prone to laying traps and have a hatred for werewolves. It isn't too inconceivable that one may have trapped the inspiration spirit in with the writer and summoned some lesser azlu into helping out, having them take over the bodies of neighbors or maybe the writer's publisher or agent so they can keep an eye out for when the werewolves start coming. We're supposed to have some stuff on them in the Idigam Chronicle book, but if you want to get a jump start the Werewolf the Forsaken book <i>Predators </i>goes into detail about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T08:24:00-08:00","id":364422,"title":"","content":"Oooh, that's good too.<br /> <br /> I've been discussing this with a friend of mine. He suggested that a competing spirit was born of the work itself (making it a spirit of the OWoD, a concept which I find fun in and of itself), and may start fighting over the writer (Inspiration-Spirit: &quot;He needs to move on to something else!&quot;; WoD-Spirit: &quot;He must continue building my world!&quot;). Has some good potential for a lot of different ways that the players could solve the situation.<br /> <br /> Still, the azlu are a great choice for a more straight-forward plot with obvious villains. And yeah, I have <i>Predators</i>, it's a great book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:54:21-08:00","id":367472,"title":"","content":"How about this:<br /> <br /> <b><i>Sar-Mussara</i><i>, </i>the All-Written Scribe</b><br /> <i>Sar-Mussara</i>, sometimes called the <i>Umpisak</i> by other spirits, is a powerful Claimed formed from the fusion of human flesh and a spirit of stories. Sar-Mussara used to subsist on the Essence drawn from writers, storytellers and the like performing their craft, and still attempts to foster and coax such humans into activity. It has determined, over its years, that the best way to do this is to place them under stress and pressure that prompt their creativity into action, regardless of deleterious results to their actual lives. For its part, the Claimed then nurtures any spirits birthed from its victims' efforts, with an interest in the long run of having them Ride their creator to form a new Claimed of stories, emotions, data or ink that it can recruit as a follower and servant.<br /> <br /> The All-Written Scribe is very old now, and has seen many a bright mind and brilliant writer come and go. The man it Claimed is actually a relatively no-name poet from years ago, forgotten by history; the poor soul was desperate enough for inspiration that he embraced the growing madness that whispered in his mind at night, letting <i>Sar-Mussara</i> take him with relative ease. The spirit itself wanted to become a Claimed because it has an obsessive need to enforce <i>narrative</i> on the world. Everything is very messy and refuses to follow proper storylines, so the All-Written Scribe intends to rectify that. Where it goes, it tries to foster strong stories in the world - it does what it can to fan the lusts of young lovers and then inflame the tensions and hatreds of their rival families and communities, provokes a man with murderous tendencies into full-blown serial killing while pushing a dogged detective to obsess over the case, and generally uses its Influences to make the world resemble a particularly twisted plot rather than letting things happen naturally. It makes heavy use of other Claimed it has 'recruited' through writers, storytellers etc, having them play particular roles to move events along or using their Influences and powers as needed.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the All-Written Scribe wishes to become the <i>totality</i> of stories. Once it has a large enough cult of Claimed minions, it intends to start boot-strapping itself up in the scale of the stories it enacts on the world, until it reaches the stage that the fate of entire nations are being affected by the narrative it weaves. Then it will consume the power and symbolism and influence of that great story to become an Incarna, becoming the greatest story ever told. Fortunately, that is a long, long way away as yet.<br /> <br /> The All-Written Scribe is a powerful old Claimed, having been Rank 3 or 4 before it latched onto its host. Despite appearing as a fairly wiry old man, the Scribe is both physically and mentally a powerhouse. Most humans will mistake the Scribe for being heavily tattooed, but an astute observer will note that the inked words and markings on the Scribe's skin appear to shift and change each day as the stories that it is tending progress. Get really close, and you can see the inky blackness of the eyes and hear the strange whispers that bubble from his open mouth even when he is not speaking; touch that paper-like skin and you can <i>feel</i> the parchment. Cut the All-Written Scribe, and watch ichor-ink flow out to splash in words on the ground. Among his powers, the Scribe can consume the words from books and computers to leave empty pages and document files; he can scratch tattoos onto victims that then worm and writhe under their skin, letting him see what they see; and he can write the life story of those whose blood he tastes, even writing out a premature ending to their existence that reality then attempts to conform to. Do not fight <i>Sar-Mussara</i> when he stands amongst books and paper; that is his chosen ground, and soon your blood will be used to write his stories. He loathes fire and storms; they are dramatically powerful for his narrative, but they easily consume the written word and stored data.<br /> <br /> Werewolves interfering with a writer he is fostering and serving as a hidden muse to are a perfect opportunity for <i>Sar-Mussara</i> to step up his game. He will try and rope in the pack to serve as part of his narrative, whether they want to or not. Pack members will find their personal lives suddenly and improbably flung into disarray by declarations of love and passion, the appearance of rivals and similar trouble. Tensions with rival packs flare up as old feuds are refreshed by dramatically-timed resurgences. An enemy previously thought defeated reappears to declare eternal vengeance. The All-Written Scribe attempts to stage-manage the stacking up of pressure on the pack through its cult of Claimed serving as actors and props, along with any other unfortunate humans its Influences can rope in. Eventually it will probably lose interest in the writer entirely and focus on the pack instead, planning to weave threads of narrative through the entire local Protectorate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T10:30:24-08:00","id":367502,"title":"","content":"You come in, use my post as a springboard, and deliver unto me an epic antagonist with fleshed-out motivation, personality, and a support network. The inspiration spirit from my original post gets fleshed out, too. Given the dramatic minefield that is my PCs' pack*, dropping this guy anywhere near them is <i>damn near perfect</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm overwhelmed to the point of speechlessness. Thank you sir. A thousand thank yous. I love these forums.<br /> <br /> *Which includes a totem of Hope, the resurgence of the Forsaken in a Pure-dominated area, a pack of scarred veterans mentoring the greenhorn PC pack, and the fact that the PCs all First Changed within the same lunar cycle. This is a <i>saga</i> in the making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}